 "notes": ["Quarters before Yahoo's 5-quarter window (the year-over-year base) and figures Yahoo's statements lack are from the company's SEC filings (XBRL company facts: 10-K / 10-Q); a fiscal Q4 is the 10-K year minus the 10-Q nine months, its diluted EPS Q4 net income / Q4 diluted shares, and EBIT / EBITDA pre-tax income + interest expense (+ depreciation & amortisation) when that matches Yahoo's own figures (computed ones are listed in \"derived\").", "Cash flow from the company's SEC filings (XBRL: operating cash flow NetCashProvidedByUsedInOperatingActivities, capex PaymentsToAcquirePropertyPlantAndEquipment), drawn as the Capex tab's SEC cash-flow table: 10-Q cash-flow figures are year-to-date, so a quarter without its own 3-month figure is the difference of two (Q2 = H1 - Q1, Q4 = full year - 9 months). FCF = operating cash flow - capex. FCF QoQ / YoY only between two positive values.", "Q1 25: computed as the fiscal year minus its other three quarters where Yahoo's quarterly statements lack them; the fields are listed in \"derived\".", "Q3 23, Q1 24, Q2 24, Q3 24: diluted EPS from Yahoo's reported EPS where it matches net income / diluted shares, else net income / diluted shares (Yahoo's statements lack it).", "Fiscal labels are the company's own fiscal year, named by the calendar year it ends in.", "PER uses the trailing 4 quarters' diluted EPS (annual: the year's), ROA the trailing 4 quarters' net income over average total assets. EPS (GAAP, diluted) is the reported figure; EPS (adjusted) is Yahoo Finance's EPS on the analysts' basis (for US companies usually the company's adjusted, non-GAAP EPS; elsewhere usually the reported one), the basis of the (E) consensus. Each has its own QoQ / YoY, so a reported figure is never compared with an adjusted one.", "Yahoo lists the adjusted EPS of the last 4 quarters only: each daily run records what it shows (market/history/financials_eps_adjusted.jsonl), so older quarters stay. A fiscal year's adjusted EPS is Yahoo's annual figure, else the sum of its four quarters when all four are known (listed in \"derived\"), else blank."]
